dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.video.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.semio.video
start body
framing record

# Video wave: REAL binary pack frame, replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope shortcut
# (`📸️snapshot/🦀️component.rs`'s old `ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`). `format u8` (real, fixed)
# then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes` (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — matches `write_str_lp`'s
# own wire exactly) are genuinely, fully described. Past that, `streams` is a HOMOGENEOUS but
# variable-length repeated record (`SemioVideoStream`, each itself holding a further
# variable-length `samples` sub-collection with an opaque `data` buffer) — the
# `protocol-array-of-records` gap (`repeat`'s own arms are tag-dispatched, not "repeat N times, N
# from a count field", for an untagged homogeneous record): modeled as one opaque trailing
# `payload` chain, the same honest boundary every P1-P3/semio pilot's own nested/recursive payload
# uses. The real Rust `encode_video_snapshot_binary`/`decode_video_snapshot_binary` stays
# genuinely, fully structured (varint counts, per-field length-prefixes, real fixed-width LE
# integers) — round-trip tested independently by this facet's own tests, only the protocol
# DESCRIPTION stops at this boundary.
header fixed 1
field format u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))

chain payload bytes
